# Line endings are LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Not a style preference. Several tests in this repository read the
# repository's own source and reason about its shape —
# `src-tauri/tests/cfg_regions.rs` splits a file on a blank line to find which
# attributes belong to which function, `architecture_claims.rs` and
# `no_dangling_docs.rs` scan for text, `workflow_parity.rs` reads YAML as
# lines. All of them are written against `\n`.
#
# Git for Windows ships with `core.autocrlf=true`, and the GitHub Actions
# Windows runner inherits it, so without this file every one of those tests is
# reading a file with `\r\n` in it that it has never seen on the machine it was
# written on. The failure that found this: `cfg_regions` reported the keystore's
# real and fake backends as carrying the same `cfg` gate, because `"\n\n"` does
# not appear in `"\r\n\r\n"` and the search window silently reached back into
# the function above.
#
# It hid behind another failure for a full round — `cargo test` stops at the
# first test binary that fails, and `agent_install` comes first alphabetically.
* text=auto eol=lf
